/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock

# Agent scratch: git worktrees for parallel task branches.
/.claude/
/.worktrees/
# Agent scratch: subagent-driven-development ledgers, briefs, review packages.
/.superpowers/

# Never commit real authentication material, even hashed.
# `tokens.json` and `*.tokens.json` do NOT match a hyphenated name such as
# `prod-tokens.json`, so `*-tokens.json` is listed separately. Without it the
# ban had a hole, and the old `!crates/*/tests/fixtures/*-tokens.json` negation
# was inert: it un-ignored files that were never ignored in the first place.
tokens.json
*.tokens.json
*-tokens.json
# The two committed test fixtures are exempted by exact path, so the exemption
# cannot widen to a real token file dropped into any crate's fixtures directory.
!crates/mecmcp-auth/tests/fixtures/junos-tokens.json
!crates/mecmcp-auth/tests/fixtures/panos-tokens.json

